 *
 * Purpose: the upstream-sync discipline (`git rebase --onto <new-tag> <old-tag> k3/implants`
 * + `--exec "make verify"`, k3_baseline_pins.md §1) needs a suite that pins the SEAMS the K3
 * implants stand on, so an upstream upgrade that silently changes one of them fails HERE with
 * a named assertion instead of failing deep inside an implant. One or more tests per seam:
 *
 *   1. kernel lifecycle    — launch → execute → dispose is a clean lifecycle; the kernel OS
 *                            process is really gone after dispose (kernel-heavy, real kernel).
 *   2. session derivation  — forkFrom copies history into an independent session; branch /
 *                            branchWithSummary move the leaf WITHOUT deleting entries
 *                            (append-only tree, the G7 lineage seam).
 *   3. compaction cut points — findCutPoint honours turn boundaries, degrades to startIndex
 *                            when no valid cut exists, and never cuts across a compaction
 *                            boundary; getLatestCompactionEntry resolves the newest cut.
